      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an organizational psychology view, your concern is very valid; prioritizing \"polish\" risks selecting for a specific, often homogenous, cultural archetype. Boards frequently reward signaling—demonstrating adherence to established power dynamics—meaning that perceived \"presence\" is often a reflection of cultural alignment rather than pure competence. However, true gravitas eventually blends both: the ability to speak persuasively (polish) is most effective when underpinned by undeniable expertise (competence).",
      "source": "target",
